      "side": 1,
      "message": "A couple of outstanding issues:\n\n1) Only lifting top-level local matrix transformations may be a good starting point, but two generalizations we may want are a) nested transformations and b) expressions on things other than coordinates. It may be tricky to generalize this current approach to support both of those needs. Perhaps we would have to handle different types of expressions each in their own way (e.g. nested coordinate transforms vs. color calculations).\n\n2) This doesn\u0027t look at the max number of varyings possible when deciding to lift expressions. Though the max number of expressions it can lift for now is 2, because it only lifts root-node-expressions.",
